# Engineering Decision Guard activation

For Travel-Companion design discussions, debugging, implementation, testing, reviews, or cross-session/agent handoffs with continuing engineering impact, search for and load the exact Skill `skills.engineering-decision-guard` before project work.

For every such task, read `docs/decisions/README.md` first, then the relevant active decisions and linked authoritative specifications. The repository is the source of truth; chat, memory, and handoff summaries are not substitutes.

**Immediate approval capture:** When the user explicitly says "定案／確定／核准／就照這個做" or clearly approves a continuing decision, that statement authorizes recording. In the same work session, create/update an Accepted record under `docs/decisions/active/`, update the index, read both back, and report the decision ID/path. Do not ask whether to record. If approved content or scope is unclear, ask only the minimum necessary question; leave it Proposed until clarified. Never claim a record exists without verified readback.

**History transition:** Never retire a decision merely because implementation/release is complete, it is old, or the AI considers it unnecessary. Move it to `docs/decisions/history/` only with explicit user approval, an explicitly approved replacement, or a verifiable objective expiry condition defined in the original decision. If uncertain, keep it Accepted and ask. Preserve the original, status, date, reason, evidence, and replacement link; update and read back the index.

A question or exploratory discussion is not implementation authority or approval to change a decision. Conflicts with Accepted decisions or scope boundaries require stopping the affected change and obtaining approval. Do not silently expand work.

Do not load for ordinary conversation, simple explanations, translations, or trivial changes with no durable engineering impact.

Loading this Skill does not replace domain specifications, AGENTS.md, Git verification, or authorization boundaries.
